y's effective\tincome\ttax\trate\tapplicable\tto\tincome\tfrom\tcontinuing\toperations (before\tnoncontrolling\tinterests\tand\tthe\tcumulative\teffect\tof\taccounting changes)\tfor\teach\tof\tthe\tperiods\tindicated\tis\tas\tfollows:\n\n|  | 2018 | 2017 | 2016 |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Federal\\tstatutory\\trate | 21.0\\t% | 35.0\\t% | 35.0\\t% |\n| State\\tincome\\ttaxes,\\tnet\\tof\\tfederal\\tbenefit | 1.8 | 1.1 | 1.8 |\n| Non-U.S.\\tincome\\ttax\\trate\\tdifferential | 5.3 | (1.6) | (3.6) |\n| Effect\\tof\\ttax\\tlaw\\tchanges(1) | (0.6) | 99.7 | — |\n| Basis\\tdifference\\tin\\taffiliates | (2.4) | (2.1) | (0.1) |\n| Tax\\tadvantaged\\tinvestments | (2.0) | (2.2) | (2.4) |\n| Other,\\tnet | (0.3) | (0.8) | (0.7) |\n| Effective\\tincome\\ttax\\trate | 22.8\\t% | 129.1\\t% | 30.0\\t% |\n\n(1) 2018\tincludes\tone-time\tTax\tReform\tbenefits\tof\t $94\tmillion\tfor\tamounts\tthat\twere considered\tprovisional\tpursuant\tto\tSAB\t118.\t2017\tincludes\tthe\tone-time\t$22,594\tmillion charge\tfor\tTax\tReform.\n\nAs\tset\tforth\tin\tthe\ttable\tabove,\tCiti's\teffective\ttax\trate\tfor\t2018\twas\t22.8% (23.3%\texcluding\tthe\teffect\tof\tprovisional\tamounts\tpursuant\tto\tSAB\t118).\tThe rate\tis\tlower\tthan\tthe\t29.8%\treported\tin\t2017\t(excluding\tthe\tone-time\timpact\tof Tax\tReform)\tprimarily\tdue\tto\tthe\tU.S.\tstatutory\trate\treduction\tfrom\t35%\tto\t21% as\tpart\tof\tTax\tReform.\n\n# Deferred\tIncome\tTaxes\n\nDeferred\tincome\ttaxes\tat\tDecember\t31\trelated\tto\tthe\tfollowing:\n\n| In\tmillions\tof\tdollars | 2018 | 2017 |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Deferred\\ttax\\tassets |  |  |\n| Credit\\tloss\\tdeduction | $3,419 | $3,423 |\n| Deferred\\tcompensation\\tand\\temployee\\tbenefits | 1,975 | 1,585 |\n| Repositioning\\tand\\tsettlement\\treserves | 428 | 454 |\n| U.S.\\ttax\\ton\\tnon-U.S.\\tearnings | 2,080 | 2,452 |\n| Investment\\tand\\tloan\\tbasis\\tdifferences | 4,891 | 3,384 |\n| Cash\\tflow\\thedges | 240 | 233 |\n| Tax\\tcred